          common Ruby web frameworks and self-hosted software.
</p> <dl class="facts" data-astro-cid-st7rnsyi> <div data-astro-cid-st7rnsyi> <dt data-astro-cid-st7rnsyi>Severity</dt> <dd data-astro-cid-st7rnsyi>Critical</dd> </div> <div data-astro-cid-st7rnsyi> <dt data-astro-cid-st7rnsyi>Fixed in</dt> <dd data-astro-cid-st7rnsyi>3.3.14, 3.4.13, 4.0.10</dd> </div> <div data-astro-cid-st7rnsyi> <dt data-astro-cid-st7rnsyi>Access needed</dt> <dd data-astro-cid-st7rnsyi>Network, no authentication</dd> </div> <div data-astro-cid-st7rnsyi> <dt data-astro-cid-st7rnsyi>CVE</dt> <dd data-astro-cid-st7rnsyi> <a href="https://www.cve.org/CVERecord?id=CVE-2026-132825" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noreferrer noopener" class="astro-st7rnsyi" data-astro-cid-st7rnsyi>CVE-2026-132825</a> <small data-astro-cid-st7rnsyi><a href="https://github.com/ruby/ruby/security/advisories/GHSA-34m4-m9fh-gqp5" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noreferrer noopener" class="astro-st7rnsyi astro-st7rnsyi" data-astro-cid-st7rnsyi>GHSA-34m4-m9fh-gqp5</a></small> </dd> </div> </dl> </div> </header> <prose-content data-astro-cid-st7rnsyi="true"> <section data-astro-cid-st7rnsyi> <h2 id="affected">Affected software <a data-heading-anchor href="#affected" aria-label="Link to this section" tabindex="-1"></a></h2> <div data-astro-cid-st7rnsyi> <h3 id="ruby">Ruby versions <a data-heading-anchor href="#ruby" aria-label="Link to this section" tabindex="-1"></a></h3> <table data-astro-cid-st7rnsyi> <thead data-astro-cid-st7rnsyi> <tr data-astro-cid-st7rnsyi> <th data-astro-cid-st7rnsyi>Ruby series</th> <th data-astro-cid-st7rnsyi>Affected</th> <th data-astro-cid-st7rnsyi>Fixed in</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody data-astro-cid-st7rnsyi> <tr data-astro-cid-st7rnsyi> <td data-astro-cid-st7rnsyi>4.0</td> <td data-astro-cid-st7rnsyi><strong data-astro-cid-st7rnsyi>4.0.0</strong> to <strong data-astro-cid-st7rnsyi>4.0.9</strong></td> <td data-astro-cid-st7rnsyi><strong data-astro-cid-st7rnsyi>4.0.10</strong></td> </tr> <tr data-astro-cid-st7rnsyi> <td data-astro-cid-st7rnsyi>3.4</td> <td data-astro-cid-st7rnsyi><strong data-astro-cid-st7rnsyi>3.4.0</strong> to <strong data-astro-cid-st7rnsyi>3.4.12</strong></td> <td data-astro-cid-st7rnsyi><strong data-astro-cid-st7rnsyi>3.4.13</strong></td> </tr> <tr data-astro-cid-st7rnsyi> <td data-astro-cid-st7rnsyi>3.3</td> <td data-astro-cid-st7rnsyi><strong data-astro-cid-st7rnsyi>3.3.0</strong> to <strong data-astro-cid-st7rnsyi>3.3.13</strong></td> <td data-astro-cid-st7rnsyi><strong data-astro-cid-st7rnsyi>3.3.14</strong></td> </tr> <tr data-astro-cid-st7rnsyi> <td data-astro-cid-st7rnsyi>3.2 and older</td> <td data-astro-cid-st7rnsyi>All releases back to <strong data-astro-cid-st7rnsyi>2.4.0</strong></td> <td data-astro-cid-st7rnsyi>EOL</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <h3 id="deployment">Frameworks <a data-heading-anchor href="#deployment" aria-label="Link to this section" tabindex="-1"></a></h3> <p data-astro-cid-st7rnsyi>
The bug is <b data-astro-cid-st7rnsyi>reachable from the following frameworks in their default configuration</b>. Other frameworks are not exposed by default, but application code that upcases strings received in a legacy encoding may also be vulnerable.
</p> <table data-astro-cid-st7rnsyi> <thead data-astro-cid-st7rnsyi> <tr data-astro-cid-st7rnsyi> <th data-astro-cid-st7rnsyi>Framework</th> <th data-astro-cid-st7rnsyi>Status on an affected Ruby</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody data-astro-cid-st7rnsyi> <tr data-astro-cid-st7rnsyi> <td data-astro-cid-st7rnsyi>Rails</td> <td data-astro-cid-st7rnsyi><span class="sev-badge high" data-astro-cid-st7rnsyi>Affected</span></td> </tr> <tr data-astro-cid-st7rnsyi> <td data-astro-cid-st7rnsyi>Sinatra (classic style)</td> <td data-astro-cid-st7rnsyi><span class="sev-badge high" data-astro-cid-st7rnsyi>Affected</span></td> </tr> <tr data-astro-cid-st7rnsyi> <td data-astro-cid-st7rnsyi>Other frameworks and plain Rack</td> <td data-astro-cid-st7rnsyi><span class="sev-badge medium" data-astro-cid-st7rnsyi>Not exposed by default</span></td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <h3 id="self-hosted">Self-hosted software <a data-heading-anchor href="#self-hosted" aria-label="Link to this section" tabindex="-1"></a></h3> <p data-astro-cid-st7rnsyi>
These products bundle their own Ruby, so the fix has to come
              from the vendor. Products marked
<span class="sev-badge high" data-astro-cid-st7rnsyi>Vulnerable</span> have no fixed
              release yet: every current version is vulnerable.
</p> <table class="products" data-astro-cid-st7rnsyi> <thead data-astro-cid-st7rnsyi> <tr data-astro-cid-st7rnsyi> <th data-astro-cid-st7rnsyi>Software</th> <th data-astro-cid-st7rnsyi>Affected versions</th> <th data-astro-cid-st7rnsyi>Fixed in</th> <th data-astro-cid-st7rnsyi>Status</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody data-astro-cid-st7rnsyi> <tr data-astro-cid-st7rnsyi> <td data-astro-cid-st7rnsyi>GitHub Enterprise Server</td> <td data-astro-cid-st7rnsyi><strong data-astro-cid-st7rnsyi>3.22.5</strong> and earlier</td> <td data-astro-cid-st7rnsyi>None</td> <td data-astro-cid-st7rnsyi><span class="sev-badge high" data-astro-cid-st7rnsyi>Vulnerable</span></td> </tr> <tr data-astro-cid-st7rnsyi> <td data-astro-cid-st7rnsyi>Chatwoot</td> <td data-astro-cid-st7rnsyi><strong data-astro-cid-st7rnsyi>4.20.0</strong> and earlier</td> <td data-astro-cid-st7rnsyi>None</td> <td data-astro-cid-st7rnsyi><span class="sev-badge high" data-astro-cid-st7rnsyi>Vulnerable</span></td> </tr> <tr data-astro-cid-st7rnsyi> <td data-astro-cid-st7rnsyi>GitLab</td> <td data-astro-cid-st7rnsyi><strong data-astro-cid-st7rnsyi>19.6.0</strong> and earlier</td> <td data-astro-cid-st7rnsyi><strong data-astro-cid-st7rnsyi>19.6.1</strong>, <strong data-astro-cid-st7rnsyi>19.5.8</strong>, <strong data-astro-cid-st7rnsyi>19.4.10</strong></td> <td data-astro-cid-st7rnsyi><span class="sev-badge low" data-astro-cid-st7rnsyi>Patched</span></td> </tr> <tr data-astro-cid-st7rnsyi> <td data-astro-cid-st7rnsyi>Mastodon</td> <td data-astro-cid-st7rnsyi><strong data-astro-cid-st7rnsyi>4.7.5</strong> and earlier</td> <td data-astro-cid-st7rnsyi><strong data-astro-cid-st7rnsyi>4.7.6</strong>, <strong data-astro-cid-st7rnsyi>4.6.12</strong>, <strong data-astro-cid-st7rnsyi>4.5.22</strong>, <strong data-astro-cid-st7rnsyi>4.4.29</strong></td> <td data-astro-cid-st7rnsyi><span class="sev-badge low" data-astro-cid-st7rnsyi>Patched</span></td> </tr> <tr data-astro-cid-st7rnsyi> <td data-astro-cid-st7rnsyi>OpenProject</td> <td data-astro-cid-st7rnsyi><strong data-astro-cid-st7rnsyi>17.9.7</strong> and earlier</td> <td data-astro-cid-st7rnsyi><strong data-astro-cid-st7rnsyi>17.9.8</strong>, <strong data-astro-cid-st7rnsyi>17.8.3</strong></td> <td data-astro-cid-st7rnsyi><span class="sev-badge low" data-astro-cid-st7rnsyi>Patched</span></td> </tr> <tr data-astro-cid-st7rnsyi> <td data-astro-cid-st7rnsyi>Discourse base image</td> <td data-astro-cid-st7rnsyi>Before <strong data-astro-cid-st7rnsyi>2.0.20261119-0203</strong></td> <td data-astro-cid-st7rnsyi><strong data-astro-cid-st7rnsyi>2.0.20261119-0203</strong></td> <td data-astro-cid-st7rnsyi><span class="sev-badge low" data-astro-cid-st7rnsyi>Patched</span></td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p class="aside" data-astro-cid-st7rnsyi>
Updated
<time datetime="2026-11-20T07:29:00.000Z" data-astro-cid-st7rnsyi>20 November 2026 at 07:29 UTC</time>.
</p> </div> </section> <section data-astro-cid-st7rnsyi> <h2 id="remediation">Remediation <a data-heading-anchor href="#remediation" aria-label="Link to this section" tabindex="-1"></a></h2> <div data-astro-cid-st7rnsyi> <h3 id="fix-deployment">Your deployment <a data-heading-anchor href="#fix-deployment" aria-label="Link to this section" tabindex="-1"></a></h3> <p data-astro-cid-st7rnsyi>
Upgrade Ruby to a fixed release:
<strong data-astro-cid-st7rnsyi>3.3.14</strong>, <strong data-astro-cid-st7rnsyi>3.4.13</strong> or
<strong data-astro-cid-st7rnsyi>4.0.10</strong>.
</p> <h3 id="fix-self-hosted">Self-hosted software <a data-heading-anchor href="#fix-self-hosted" aria-label="Link to this section" tabindex="-1"></a></h3> <p data-astro-cid-st7rnsyi>
Install the vendor's fixed release. See
<a href="#self-hosted" data-astro-cid-st7rnsyi>Self-hosted software</a> for fixed versions
              of popular products.
</p> </div> </section> <section data-astro-cid-st7rnsyi> <h2 id="details">Technical details <a data-heading-anchor href="#details" aria-label="Link to this section" tabindex="-1"></a></h2> <div data-astro-cid-st7rnsyi> <h3 id="root-cause">Root cause <a data-heading-anchor href="#root-cause" aria-label="Link to this section" tabindex="-1"></a></h3> <p data-astro-cid-st7rnsyi>
Most of Ruby's single-byte encodings have no capital
<code data-astro-cid-st7rnsyi>ß</code>. Upcasing it writes two bytes, <code data-astro-cid-st7rnsyi>SS</code>, but
              the loop only bounds-checks one (<code data-astro-cid-st7rnsyi>to &lt; to_end</code>).
</p> <div class="expressive-code"><style>.expressive-code{font-family:var(--ec-uiFontFml);font-size:var(--ec-uiFontSize);font-weight:var(--ec-uiFontWg);line-height:var(--ec-uiLineHt);text-size-adjust:none;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none}.expressive-code *:not(:is(svg, svg *)){all:revert;box-sizing:border-box}.expressive-code pre{display:flex;margin:0;padding:0;border:var(--ec-brdWd) solid var(--ec-brdCol);border-radius:calc(var(--ec-brdRad) + var(--ec-brdWd));background:var(--ec-codeBg)}.expressive-code pre:focus-visible{outline:3px solid var(--ec-focusBrd);outline-offset:-3px}.expressive-code pre > code{all:unset;display:block;flex:1 0 100%;padding:var(--ec-codePadBlk) 0;color:var(--ec-codeFg);font-family:var(--ec-codeFontFml);font-size:var(--ec-codeFontSize);font-weight:var(--ec-codeFontWg);line-height:var(--ec-codeLineHt)}.expressive-code pre{overflow-x:auto}.expressive-code pre.wrap .ec-line .code{white-space:pre-wrap;overflow-wrap:break-word;min-width:min(20ch, var(--ecMaxLine, 20ch))}.expressive-code pre.wrap .ec-line .code span.indent{white-space:pre}.expressive-code pre::-webkit-scrollbar,.expressive-code pre::-webkit-scrollbar-track{background-color:inherit;border-radius:calc(var(--ec-brdRad) + var(--ec-brdWd));border-top-left-radius:0;border-top-right-radius:0}.expressive-code pre::-webkit-scrollbar-thumb{background-color:var(--ec-sbThumbCol);border:4px solid transparent;background-clip:content-box;border-radius:10px}.expressive-code pre::-webkit-scrollbar-thumb:hover{background-color:var(--ec-sbThumbHoverCol)}.expressive-code .ec-line{direction:ltr;unicode-bidi:isolate;display:grid;grid-template-areas:'gutter code';grid-template-columns:auto 1fr;position:relative}.expressive-code .ec-line .gutter{grid-area:gutter;color:var(--ec-gtrFg)}.expressive-code .ec-line .gutter > *{pointer-events:none;user-select:none;-webkit-user-select:none}.expressive-code .ec-line .gutter ~ .code{--ecLineBrdCol:var(--ec-gtrBrdCol)}.expressive-code .ec-line.highlight .gutter{color